{"strongs": "H6311", "word": "פֹּה", "translit": "poh", "root": "פה", "morph": "H:Adv", "pos": "adverb of location", "gloss": "here, hither", "definition": "פֹּה 58 , and ( Ezek 40:1-41:200 , 23 out of 35 t.) פּוֺ , also Job 38:11 b פֹּא , adverb of location here, hither (probably from the same demonstrative √ found in so, then (often in apodosis), אַף , אֵפוֺא : compare Kö ii. l, 247 f., 243, 331 f. ): — 1. here: \\ \\ a. Gen 19:12 עֹד מִילְֿךָ פֹּה whom hast thou still here ? Gen 22:5 שְׁבוּ לָכֶם פֹּה , Gen 40:15 ; Num 22:8 ; Num 32:16 ; Deut 5:28 ; Deut 12:8 ; Judg 4:20 הֲיֵשׁ פֹּה אִישׁ , 2Kgs 3:11 , etc.; asked in some surprise, Judg 18:3 מַהלְּֿךָ פֹה = what is thy business here ? simil. 1Kgs 19:9 ; 1Kgs 19:13 ; Isa 22:16 ; Isa 52:5 וְעַתָּה מַהלִּֿיפֹֿה . compare the synonym בָּזֶה , כֹּה 2. b. עַדפֹּֿה Job 38:11 a. \\ \\ c. מִפֹּה or מִפּוֺ , only Ezek 40-41, and always (except Ezek 40:12 a, where it must be supplied with ᵐ5 ᵑ6 ) repeated, on this side ... on that side (compare מִזֶּה ֗֗֗ מִזֶּה ), Ezek 40:10 (twice in verse); Ezek 40:12 b; Ezek 40:21 (twice in verse), etc. \\ \\ d. with the interrogative אֵי , אֵיפֹה where ? . 2. after a verb of motion, hither , 1Sam 16:11 עַדבּֿאֹוֺ פֹה , Ezra 4:2 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6537')\">BDB6537</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H6311')\">H6311</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6536')\">BDB6536</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6538')\">BDB6538</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>פֹּה</bdbheb><sub>58</sub>, and (<ref ref=\"Ezek 40:1-41:200\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"40\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"200\" onclick=\"bcv(26,40,1)\">Ezek 40:1-41:200</ref>, 23 out of 35 t.) <bdbheb>פּוֺ</bdbheb>, also <ref ref=\"Job 38:11\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"38\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"38\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(18,38,11)\">Job 38:11</ref>b <bdbheb>פֹּא</bdbheb>, <b>adverb of location</b> <highlightword>here, hither</highlightword> (probably from the same demonstrativ